    "text_full": "Skip to content\nAbout Us\nPrograms\nNews & Media\nDONATE\nFR\nHERITAGE MINUTES\nPODCASTS\nVIDEOS\nEDUCATION GUIDES\nSEARCH PRODUCTIONS\nHome\n / Podcasts / Record of Service Podcast\nRecord of Service Podcast\n\nRecord of Service, a podcast presented by The Memory Project. In this series, we bring you interviews with Canada’s veterans—their stories of life, loss and service. \n\nFeatures\nEpisode 1: Codebreakers\nPopular\nThousands of women served in intelligence facilities like Britain’s Bletchley Park and Canada’s Camp X during the Second World War.\nEpisode 5: D-Day\nStaff Pick\nJune 6, 2019 marked the 75th anniversary of the Allied landings in Normandy, France during the Second World War.\nAll (5) Episodes\nSort by:\nDate\nA to Z\nSearch & Filter\nEpisode 5: D-Day\n2019\nEpisode 4: The Prisoner\n2019\nEpisode 3: The Tomkins Brothers\n2019\nEpisode 2: Do No Harm\n2019\nEpisode 1: Codebreakers\n2019\n\nHistorica Canada is a charitable organization that offers programs in both official languages that you can use to explore, learn, reflect on our history, and consider what it means to be Canadian.\n\nHistorica Canada's business number is 885434720RR0001\n\nAbout Us\nPolicies\nCareers\nHistorica Canada Content Usage Request Form\n\nFollow Us\nMore From Historica Canada\nCitizenship Challenge\nHeritage Minutes\nThe Memory Project\nThe Canadian Encyclopedia\nPartnership: The World Remembers\n© Historica Canada 2026. All rights reserved.\nWebsite by DS"
